{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The target argues against the panel via 'fragmentation loss' but provides no causal mechanism linking checklist-driven decomposition to the specific outcome reliability metric. The problem demands a mechanism distinguishing genuine reliability gain from mere checklist compliance; the target asserts non-experts 'fail to see' contradictions but offers no causal explanation for why the expert's compressed pattern recognition would be more reliable on objectively verifiable outcomes rather than merely phenomenologically different.","target":"01271dc2543ff3829368b029f1b3c075a7797682284bd049f82a1782ee62ba62"},{"attack":true,"case":"The claim rests on 'threshold-sensing' requiring infinitely long checklists, but this is not a causal mechanism—it is an unboundedness assertion. The target provides no evidence that objectively verifiable outcomes in practice depend on threshold phenomena that resist finite Boolean decomposition. The countercondition admits gestalt can be fully mapped into finite Boolean logic gates, which directly contradicts the 'infinitely long' premise, yet the target offers no mechanism for determining which class of tasks falls on which side, failing the problem's reliability-gain-vs-compliance distinction.","target":"24bb0f62586e881a875e98e7697df433163d08101d2f6703133584180f294b11"},{"attack":true,"case":"The 'explanation effect' mechanism claims forced verbalization converts System 1 to System 2 reasoning, simulating higher expertise. But the target provides no causal basis for why pseudo-expert scrutiny via non-expert consensus would be MORE reliable than actual expert intuition rather than merely approximating it. The mechanism explains how the panel might reach expert-adjacent performance, not why it would exceed it on average—which is the claim the problem asks to argue for or against. Additionally, the target does not address what evidence within a single evaluation would distinguish this genuine gain from checklist compliance tracking the right answer, leaving the problem's central diagnostic question unanswered.","target":"6897dd81d5214f6b84d36ae12657c31cbd68c4ea82221dbad232e2461e581291"},{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"8d2fe09576f512bbb1e37b2c0d7c5c10f2be6a89f71f1107a7883bec09822c1a"}]}